WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.403
-My first guest is a
Grammy-winning artist

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:05.105
who has a
new documentary coming out

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:08.441
this Friday on
Amazon Prime Video called

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:10.543
"P!nk: All I Know So Far."

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:13.880
Please welcome
the one-and-only P!nk!

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:14.948
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:18.017
Ah! It's so good to see you.
Hi, bud!

00:00:18.017 --> 00:00:19.719
-Hi!

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:20.886
-Oh, I love you.

00:00:20.886 --> 00:00:22.921
Aww! Thanks for the hug.
I love it.

00:00:22.921 --> 00:00:25.491
You know, we were talking about
you pretty recently,

00:00:25.491 --> 00:00:28.461
because we had
Steve Buscemi on the show,

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:29.762
and he was explain--

00:00:29.762 --> 00:00:33.032
He told me some story
that sounded pretty insane.

00:00:33.032 --> 00:00:35.468
This is --
When you first started out,

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:36.836
you ran up to him,
'cause, obviously, he was

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:39.338
Mr. Pink in "Reservoir Dogs."

00:00:39.338 --> 00:00:43.243
And he said he thinks you came
up to him and said like,

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:45.311
"You don't understand,
but I'm named after you,

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:46.546
and I'm going to be
big one day."

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:47.914
Or something.

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:50.449
He was freaking out about buying
a gift or something for --

00:00:50.449 --> 00:00:51.584
He had a big, long story,

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:52.618
but he was so embarrassed.

00:00:52.618 --> 00:00:53.786
And he thinks it was you,

00:00:53.786 --> 00:00:56.088
and he never got
a chance to apologize to you.

00:00:56.088 --> 00:00:57.089
Do you know what
I'm talking about?

00:00:57.089 --> 00:00:58.424
And is this a real story?

00:00:58.424 --> 00:01:00.793
-Oh, I -- No, it's a real story.

00:01:00.793 --> 00:01:05.965
But to be fair, I ran at him
on a New York street.

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:09.669
I physically -- I'm like
a hummingbird with my love.

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:11.337
I'm very aggressive.
-Okay.

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:13.706
-And I was just this pink --

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:15.474
I remember I was
dressed in, like, all --

00:01:15.474 --> 00:01:16.776
a silver ensemble

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:18.611
and I had short, pink hair
and a tongue ring.

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:20.947
And I just --
"You're Steve Buscemi

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:23.216
and you're Mr. Pink
and I'm P!nk and you're pink

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:25.451
and I'm going to be so famous

00:01:25.451 --> 00:01:27.287
and I just love you
and then I got my --"

00:01:27.287 --> 00:01:29.989
And he's like, "What the [bleep]

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:32.892
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:34.527
He was like, "Aah!"

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:36.329
I would have reacted
that way, too.

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:38.798
It was a lot.
It was a lot.

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:39.832
-That's so funny.

00:01:39.832 --> 00:01:42.668
And you haven't seen
each other since?

00:01:42.668 --> 00:01:45.738
-No. I mean, All this time,
for like 20 years,

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:47.540
I was like, "That guy hates me."

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.541
-Oh, my gosh.

00:01:49.541 --> 00:01:51.644
Well, anyway, he was embarrassed
and he was like --

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:54.147
because, obviously,
we know who you are now.

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:58.351
If you don't,
you're living under a rock.

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:00.086
This weekend --
You have a huge weekend.

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:03.990
You're getting the Icon Award
at the Billboard...

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:05.157
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:05.157 --> 00:02:08.294
...at the
Billboard Music Awards.

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:10.162
Just don't listen for a second.

00:02:10.162 --> 00:02:11.631
I just want to let
everyone know who else --

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:14.901
This has only been
given out 10 times.

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:17.269
Here's the people on the list.

00:02:17.269 --> 00:02:21.841
Celine Dion, Mariah Carey, Cher,
Janet Jackson, Garth Brooks,

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:25.678
Jennifer Lopez,
Stevie Wonder, and Prince.

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:28.982
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:30.349
P!nk!

00:02:30.349 --> 00:02:31.683
-That's a lot of pressure.

00:02:31.683 --> 00:02:34.253
At first, I was like,
"Oh, it's the old-lady award.

00:02:34.253 --> 00:02:37.757
I'm getting the old-lady award.
They want me to go."

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:39.892
-No, it's unbelievable.
-But, no, it's amazing!

00:02:39.892 --> 00:02:42.128
I read the names, I was like,
"They got this wrong.

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:44.596
There's so many other names
that should be there."

00:02:44.596 --> 00:02:46.065
-No.
-It's a huge honor.

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:48.768
And anytime they give me
eight minutes to perform,

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:50.236
I'm like, "Oh, it's on."

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:51.604
-Yeah.

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:54.106
-So, I'm very, very --
I'm probably looking forward to

00:02:54.106 --> 00:02:58.010
this performance more than
I have looked forward to one

00:02:58.010 --> 00:02:59.111
in a very long time.

00:02:59.111 --> 00:03:00.547
I'm very nervous.

00:03:00.547 --> 00:03:02.514
-I don't know how many people
come up to me and say like,

00:03:02.514 --> 00:03:03.683
"Have you ever seen P!nk live?"

00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:05.084
And I go, "Yeah."

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:07.486
And they go, "It's the best
concert I've ever been to.

00:03:07.486 --> 00:03:09.788
It's amazing."
-Aww! That makes me so happy.

00:03:09.788 --> 00:03:13.025
I'm terrible at a lot of things,
but I can perform.

00:03:13.025 --> 00:03:15.728
-Yeah, you can. That's right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:18.665
That's exactly correct.

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:19.765
And I love this, by the way.

00:03:19.765 --> 00:03:21.935
"P!nk: All I Know So Far:
SetList,"

00:03:21.935 --> 00:03:24.504
your first-ever live album.

00:03:24.504 --> 00:03:26.105
I love the name.

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:27.573
-Yeah, thank you.

00:03:27.573 --> 00:03:29.809
-You never wanted to do
a live album.

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:32.078
-Nope. I never wanted to do
a documentary either,

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:34.213
but here we are.

00:03:34.213 --> 00:03:36.315
-Well, I'm glad you did,
because now you're on the show.

00:03:36.315 --> 00:03:37.483
This is fantastic.

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:38.718
Gives us something
to talk about.

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:39.752
But, yeah --

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:41.820
-I just miss --
I miss live music.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:43.689
And it's just --
I think we all do.

00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:45.524
I miss sweating with strangers.

00:03:45.524 --> 00:03:51.164
And I listened to this set list
all the way through

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:53.433
and I just felt
so good at the end.

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:56.368
I think a lot of people --
still, after 20 years,

00:03:56.368 --> 00:04:02.208
think I'm just this man-hating,
obnoxious, loud --

00:04:02.208 --> 00:04:03.742
"So what?! Rah!"

00:04:03.742 --> 00:04:09.215
But we do so many fun covers
and so many genres of music.

00:04:09.215 --> 00:04:13.085
And there's Queen covers
and "Time After Time."

00:04:13.085 --> 00:04:15.955
And I just felt really happy.

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:17.456
One of the --
We do "We Are the Champions"

00:04:17.456 --> 00:04:18.924
at Rock in Rio in Brazil,

00:04:18.924 --> 00:04:20.526
and I was just
instantly back there

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:24.163
with 100,000 people
sweating and happy.

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:27.166
And it just makes me feel good.
The record makes me feel good.

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:29.635
-P!nk, who directed this, again?

00:04:29.635 --> 00:04:31.637
-Michael Gracey, from
"The Greatest Showman."

00:04:31.637 --> 00:04:34.840
-Yeah. Michael Gracey,
"Greatest Showman."

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:37.710
Amazing director.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:40.612
And I think, if I were you,
I would be like,

00:04:40.612 --> 00:04:41.947
"Document everything,"

00:04:41.947 --> 00:04:44.851
because you put on these shows
that are like "Whew!"

00:04:44.851 --> 00:04:46.585
Do you get a chance to ever
look at your work

00:04:46.585 --> 00:04:48.053
and you're like,
"Oh, yeah, I did that.

00:04:48.053 --> 00:04:49.222
That was pretty cool."

00:04:49.222 --> 00:04:51.490
-Yeah, I don't experience
things in real time.

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:52.958
It takes me a while.

00:04:52.958 --> 00:04:54.893
I look back
and then I'm like, "Oh, wow.

00:04:54.893 --> 00:04:57.196
Like, I hung from the side
of a building.

00:04:57.196 --> 00:04:58.430
Why?"

00:04:58.430 --> 00:05:01.834
But with this --
with this documentary,

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:03.336
I was like, You know what?

00:05:03.336 --> 00:05:07.373
As kids, you narrate your life
and you tell these stories,

00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:08.874
like, about your childhood,

00:05:08.874 --> 00:05:11.143
and everybody had a terrible
childhood in some way.

00:05:11.143 --> 00:05:13.712
And "My mom locked me in a
closet, I'm sure of it,

00:05:13.712 --> 00:05:15.147
and I was never fed."

00:05:15.147 --> 00:05:18.685
And so whatever stories
my kids come up with about me,

00:05:18.685 --> 00:05:23.656
this documentary will prove that
they're not telling the truth.

00:05:23.656 --> 00:05:25.758
-That's the whole reason
for doing this.

00:05:25.758 --> 00:05:28.260
So that they can see mommy
was always loving

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:29.395
and gave you a great life.

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:31.730
-That's it.
-See? You need that, yeah.

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:36.936
So, yeah, lawyer up.
That's fantastic.

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:39.005
We love you.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:39.005 --> 00:05:41.207
-Here's P!nk
in her new documentary,

00:05:41.207 --> 00:05:43.776
"All I Know So Far" --
Amazon Prime Video.

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:45.010
Take a look.

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:49.615
♪♪

00:05:49.615 --> 00:05:51.984
-They grew up with
the hotels and the jets

00:05:51.984 --> 00:05:53.752
and the never having to
worry about things

00:05:53.752 --> 00:05:55.120
like money and safety.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:58.657
And I'm their mom, I'm their
friend, but one day --

00:05:58.657 --> 00:06:01.994
you know, one day, they're going
to see through all of it.

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:03.762
They're going to see the act.

00:06:03.762 --> 00:06:05.297
They're going to see
through the strength

00:06:05.297 --> 00:06:08.334
and they're going to find
the truth underneath, I hope.

00:06:08.334 --> 00:06:10.236
And they're going to
discover little Alecia,

00:06:10.236 --> 00:06:12.471
who's still hiding in here,

00:06:12.471 --> 00:06:14.806
who's still learning
how to heal.

00:06:14.806 --> 00:06:18.744
And I just hope they have
the grace and the heart

00:06:18.744 --> 00:06:22.314
to accept my mortality
and to accept that I'm human,

00:06:22.314 --> 00:06:23.416
like them.

00:06:23.416 --> 00:06:25.418
And then they'll have
their own kids,

00:06:25.418 --> 00:06:29.388
and so the cycle continues,
all of it.

00:06:29.388 --> 00:06:31.457
-Flying through Wembley.

00:06:31.457 --> 00:06:34.293
Flying through Wembley.
So cool.

00:06:34.293 --> 00:06:36.229
P!nk, everybody!
[ Cheers and applause ]

